# Source-archive SHA256 checksums for this repository's own release tags.
#
# Format: HASH  IDENTIFIER
# (two spaces between hash and identifier, like sha256sum output)
#
# This file is an audit trail for the source bundle a release publishes. The
# required provenance source is the release manifest, which records the digest
# of the bundle the release workflow built from the released commit. The entry
# here lets a reviewed, independent re-download of the published bundle
# confirm later that the bytes still match.
#
# Record an entry after the tag is published, with the maintainer script (the
# entry lands in a later commit, so the tag's own tree is unaffected):
#   bash packaging/scripts/record-source-archive-digest.sh v0.9.2
# The script downloads the published source bundle by default. Pass
# --github-archive only for releases published before the workflow built its
# own bundle. It never overwrites a differing entry.
#
# The release workflow compares any recorded entry with the digest of the
# bundle it built and fails on disagreement. A missing entry does not block a
# tag release or warn during it.
#
# Identifier convention: source-<tag>          (e.g. source-v0.9.2)
